  "summary": "At DevDay Exchange in Berlin, OpenAI mostly repeated what it had already announced, but it did share a few new details. The AI assistant Dots should roll out more widely in Europe \"in a few weeks,\" and weekly Codex users in Germany have grown twentyfold since January. A clear subtext ran through the sessions and the repeated nods to ChatGPT's 1.2 billion weekly users: OpenAI wants developers to build their businesses directly on its infrastructure. The article OpenAI teases Dots for Europe, but its Berlin DevDay was really about building a platform appeared first on The Decoder .",
